# src/ git handling
# DEFAULT (Option B): one repo — Claude config AND src/ code are tracked and pushed together.
# src/ commits normally; nothing to do here.
#
# Caveat: if src/ was cloned from another repo it carries its own .git, which cannot be tracked
# inside this repo. To fold it in, remove src/.git first (this drops the old remote/history link).
#
# Option A (alternative): keep src/ as its own repo with its own remote, and don't push the
# workspace. Uncomment the next line so this repo ignores src/ entirely:
# src/
